; setquad_index_out_of_range: an out-of-range quadratic write must raise.
;
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's SETQUAD row already said "Error: IndexOutOfBounds if
; indices out of range [0, size)" and the Rust VM did not do it: the write
; landed in the sparse map and the program halted clean, leaving a
; 4-variable model carrying a coefficient on variable 9. xqvm_py raised.
;
; The out-of-range operand is i here and j in getquad_index_out_of_range, so
; the pair covers both sides. Neither index equals the other and neither
; equals the size, so nothing passes by coincidence.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 9           ; i, past the extent
PUSH 1           ; j, in range
PUSH 7           ; value
SETQUAD r0
HALT
